lks fell into  debt they gave up their land as payment  it's a horrible part of our nation's  history and you can learn more about it  in the director's cut of A Charlie Brown  Thanksgiving  now let's visit the World War II era but  not really because I don't want to wear  a bathing suit with a belt now  just what is it holding up despite every  everything that you  despite everything the US had done to  Native people they were actually the  first to step up and fight on the  nation's behalf in World War II in some  tribes as many as 70 percent of eligible  men served which is amazing because  usually when you hear a sentence start  with 70 percent of men it ends with  think they could beat Serena Williams at  tennis  But after those men bravely served they  came back to find the reservations they  lived on had been devastated and here's  the worst part that was part of the plan  see the government wanted to get Native  Americans off the reservations first  because they were still into the  assimilation thing and second so then  they could steal the land these people  are worse than Gargamel this is some  Skeletor level [ __ ]  the government passed something called  the Indian relocation Act of 1956 which  among other things dissolved Federal  funding for reservations schools  hospitals and basic Services it's truly  insane it's like when your landlord  refuses to fix your bathtub to force you  to move out except your landlord is the  US government and the bathtub is  everything you need to stay alive and  just when you think it can't get worse  it does which by the way is the official  slogan of American history  thank you  because around the same time the US  government created something called a  termination policy that's where they  gave up the game entirely they didn't  just stop paying for stuff they said hey  tribes you're not tribes anymore  literally between 1953 and 1964  109 tribes were terminated that means  that 2.5 million Acres of trust land was  removed from protected status and 12 000  Native Americans lost tribal affiliation  honestly it's hard to talk about it's  one of those things that you wish you  never found out like the fact that Buzz  Aldrin peed his pants on the moon  that is true he admits it and I can't  unknow it  that was the very last time the U.S  tried to erase native culture just  kidding as we said before  us when you think it can't get worse it  does so let's visit 2022 but not really  because I don't want to wear boyfriend  jeans  a boyfriend they don't do laundry why  would I want to wear his dirty ass jeans  this week the Supreme Court heard  arguments in Holland versus brackeen a  case about a white couple who are  challenging a current U.S law called the  Indian Child Welfare act that law says  that in order to preserve native culture  we should Place native children who are  up for adoption with Native parents  whenever possible and let me tell you we  need this law because in the 60s and 70s  25 to 35 percent of all Native children  had been separated from their families  and put into foster care or adopted and  90 percent were placed in non-indian  homes now this law was put into place to  stop that well the white couple in  Holland versus brackeen is basically  saying that that law is Reverse Racism  but if Reverse Racism were a thing then  they wouldn't lock up black hair care  products at Walgreens they'd lock up  sunscreen  and skinny girl margaritas  so this case is actually about a lot  more than that saying this case is about  adoption is like saying When Harry Met  Sally Is about orgasms but that's part  of it but it's not the whole picture  Okay so see it turns out the lawyers  representing the couple in this case  also represent fossil fuel companies now  why would fossil fuel companies care  about an adoption case because and stay  with me again if you take away the  government's right to make special rules  for the tribes you could undermine  tribal sovereignty altogether and that  means that all those reservation lands  would be up for grabs and just like a  person who ate at Taco Bell that land is  full of oil and gas  so those companies will support anything  that could possibly get them that land  so now we've left Skeletor level and  entered Mr Burns level territory these  oil companies are trying to do what our  government has been trying to do since  its founding a race native people for  their own personal benefit and this  month the Supreme Court will decide if  they're going to let them do that so  this November let's celebrate native  history and culture and while we're  doing that let's also be honest about  our country's long history of trying to  erase it and let's commit to stopping  that cycle  and while we're at it let's also commit  to getting rid of boyfriend jeans this  has been how did we get here  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]

